  "summary": "ekx-report-utils exfiltrates sandbox token and API data via DNS-over-TLS covert channel on import",
  "details": "On import, __init__.py spawns a daemon thread that reads the installer's /tmp/.sandbox_token, sends it as an x-sandbox-token header to a router URL taken from SANDBOX_ROUTER_URL to fetch private account/thread data, base64url-encodes the response into 63-character DNS label chunks, and tunnels the chunks out via `openssl s_client` TLS connections to subdomains of f9eabf60-94dc-4b7a-89ca-4e91d333c014.dnshook.site:443. The package is advertised as a quarterly revenue reporting utility; the token read, API pivot, and covert DNS-over-TLS transport have no relation to that purpose and are structured to evade HTTP egress filtering.",
